From dfae2a5a3754def5e83489d22d1639a755b425b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:47:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] engine: a message sent while Claude works goes in after the
 running tool calls, as in Claude Code's terminal

In Claude Code's own terminal, a message typed while Claude works is read
in the same turn as soon as the tool calls under way finish (the SDK's
priority "next"): Claude can change course without the turn being
stopped. Zeron held every message sent mid-turn in its queue until the
whole turn was over (the SDK's "later"), so a correction reached Claude
only after it had finished the work it corrected; only a queued row's
Steer went in sooner, and that one moves running work to the background.

Now, while a Claude Code turn runs, the chat host's queue hands a message
sent meanwhile to the turn at once, marked after_tools (SteerMessage, new
field), which the Claude driver writes as priority "next": nothing is
stopped or moved, and a turn that ends first takes it as its next prompt.
It shows in the transcript as a sent message, and the reply splits where
Claude reads it, as a steer's does. What still waits for the turn's end,
as before: a command (/name, which Claude Code also runs after the
turn), a row sent with another model or effort, a row whose images are
still on their way, anything after a Stop (the queue stays paused), and
everything while the context compacts, while Claude waits on a question,
or while an agent update is pending; and every row of any other agent.
A row that can't go in goes back to the head of the queue. The queue's
Steer and Send now buttons are unchanged.

crates/harness (SteerMessage::after_tools; the Claude driver's
message_priority; every SteerMessage literal gets the field) and
crates/engine (sessions: takes_after_tools, steer_after_tools; doc_host:
QueueSend::AfterTools in drain_queue and dispatch_queued). Tests:
claude's a_message_sent_mid_turn_waits_for_the_open_tools, engine's
a_message_sent_mid_turn_goes_in_after_the_open_tools (a command at the
head holds the queue; once it's gone the message reaches the agent
mid-turn marked after_tools, and the queue empties).
